WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.320
Big changes are in store for fans of The Walking
Dead.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.200
In season 9, the series will lose stars Andrew
Lincoln and Lauren Cohan, and a new showrunner

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.420
steps in to take the story to new places.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.360
Do these alterations bode well for the AMC
series?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.120
No one knows yet, but a slew of theories and
rumors have hinted at where The Walking Dead

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:17.800
will go next.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.660
Let's unpack the details.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.580
Two brothers fighting

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.420
Rick and Daryl's camaraderie has been a core
part of the show for years, but that might

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.080
not be the case in season 9.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.420
Rumors have been swirling that Daryl and Rick's
bromance might be compromised over Rick's

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.980
controversial decision to spare Negan's life.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.390
Does this mean the two will become enemies
before Rick's final bow?

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.840
Not according to Norman Reedus:

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:45.280
"They fight and they disagree on things but
it's like two brothers fighting, they always

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.260
have each other's back but they don't necessarily
agree on everything."

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.000
A second time jump

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.220
According to UPROXX, rumors are circulating
regarding two shifts in time for season 9:

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.820
one of a couple years and another longer one
of four or five years.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:04.739
The second time jump could help further the
decayed tone new showrunner Angela Kang previously

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:06.700
teased to Entertainment Weekly, saying,

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.590
"We'll explore what happened as man-made objects
and structures break down.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.480
Infrastructure like roads and bridges are
changing and crumbling.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.460
And we'll also explore what happens as resources
are getting low."

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.320
New loves

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.720
Along with a hefty bump in pay, Reedus will
receive top billing once Andrew Lincoln makes

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.280
his exit.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.720
With that sort of scrutiny, it's hard not
to wonder if fans will finally see Daryl make

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.439
a love connection in season 9.

00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:35.110
There are many theories, rumors, and requests
regarding Daryl's future, from a deeper connection

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.189
to Carol to a brand new love interest.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:42.000
The Hollywood Reporter even posed a compelling
possibility: what if Daryl finds a man to

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:42.500
love?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.260
The trade suggested a love connection between
him and Aaron.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.700
"Whether we make it or not, we do it together.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.000
We have to."

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.000
He's not the only one with a possible new
romance; the Nerdist has theorized that Alden,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.281
one of the reformed Saviors, might be the
tv version of the comics' Dante—which might

00:02:04.281 --> 00:02:07.320
mean that he could be a new romantic partner
for Maggie.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.880
One definitely confirmed love story is between
Carol and King Ezekiel.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.330
Photos from the new season showed Carol and
the king sharing a tender moment, and a subsequent

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.460
trailer shows the two sharing a smooch.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.420
Father Gabriel's second sight

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:24.730
After the trials he endured in season 8, it's
looking like Father Gabriel will step confidently

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.680
into the role of holy man once the new episodes
premiere.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.280
Leaked images reveal Gabriel, who looks to
be completely blind in one eye, donning a

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.460
classic-looking Southern preacher outfit.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.030
Whatever he lacks in physical sight, he may
make up for with religious clarity.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:42.800
According to BleedingCool, Gabriel will be
the one helping Jadis transition to her new

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.040
home in Alexandria.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.900
A new leader

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.500
With Rick's death presumably looming, speculation
regarding Daryl's leadership role has grown,

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.980
but as Norman Reedus told TVLine, the rumors
of Daryl taking over for Rick are just not

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:56.480
true.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.840
"That's not a true story.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.280
Rick is the quarterback of this football team,
he's always been, he always will…"

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.080
So if Daryl won't be taking over as leader,
who will?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.500
Well, there's been a worthy successor under
our noses this entire time.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.300
Rick himself has already said who he wants
to take over for him as leader if anything

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:13.800
happens:

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.780
"And if it's me who doesn't make it, you're
going to have to lead the others forward.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.120
Because you're the one who can."

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:26.440
It's an idea that's backed up by what Angela
Kang told EW about the female characters.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.840
"We're going to see our women really step
up.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.770
And we're gonna show a lot of stories about
leadership with Maggie, with Michonne, with

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.260
Carol.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:36.660
And they're gonna go toe to toe with each
other and with our men."

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.160
Unfortunately, if Michonne does step up as
leader, it may not be forever.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.960
Danai Gurira's star is steadily on the rise
with plenty of movie roles, which puts her

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.900
continued Walking Dead future in question.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.160
When pressed on Michonne's future in Alexandria,
the new showrunner said Gurira is "definitely

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.580
a series regular this season."

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.160
As for what happens after season 9, though,
Kang said plainly, "that is out of my realm."

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.300
A new bat, man

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.960
The question of how Rick Grimes will be written
out of The Walking Dead's ninth season still

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:05.720
looms large.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:06.760
Will he live?

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:07.640
Will he die?

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.760
Will he simply wander off into the wilderness
to allow for cameos in later seasons?

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.860
Lincoln has confirmed that he's coming back
with the intention of directing an episode

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.060
in Season 10, but as for an actual appearance
as Rick?

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:18.960
No one knows.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:23.140
But one thing we do know is that he'll be
using the time he has left to brutalize some

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:28.180
more zombies with a shiny new weapon inspired
by none other than his arch-nemesis Negan.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:32.939
Promotional materials for the new season show
a grey-bearded Rick Grimes toying with a bat-like

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:33.440
weapon.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.960
From the show's previews, it's clear he knows
just how to use it, too.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.340
A dead deputy returns

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.460
Of all the long-lost characters who could
be brought back into The Walking Dead's fold

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:48.199
for season 9, the return of Jon Bernthal's
Shane was probably the least expected.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:53.020
After all, he's been dead for over six seasons,
and Bernthal has had plenty of other roles

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.550
to keep him busy in the meantime.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:59.370
However, the actor was spotted near the Atlanta,
Georgia area during the season's summer production.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.340
His appearance set off a rash of speculation
that he might be making a cameo as Lincoln

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.340
preps for his exit.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:08.640
Bernthal's return to the show was confirmed
soon after, though the exact details of his

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.780
role reprisal have been kept close to the
vest.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:12.720
Frenemies

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.199
Rick's decision to let Negan live after the
All Out War with the Saviors might come back

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.780
to bite him in more ways than one.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.240
Not only has he earned the ire of his friends
with this moment of undeserved mercy, but

00:05:24.241 --> 00:05:26.610
now he's going to have to actually deal with
Negan.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:30.590
Although, Kang has revealed that the former
enemies might have a lot more in common than

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:31.590
one might expect.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:36.419
"Rick goes down there and it's part therapy
and part gloating, like they're just trying

00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:38.020
to work their way through it.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.020
They both feel, in some ways, like dinosaurs
after the war."

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.539
Rick has already been known to have trouble
making solid leadership decisions in the past,

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:49.720
so one has to imagine that having Negan in
his ear probably won't be too helpful.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:51.940
Maggie's happy ending?

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:56.499
Even though Cohan will be departing the show,
things might just be looking up for Maggie

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.480
in the new season.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:01.880
The previews for season 9 show that her baby
will finally join the world after so many

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.380
seasons of Maggie's pregnancy.

00:06:03.849 --> 00:06:07.680
With Lauren Cohan's impending exit from the
series ahead though, fans might be tempted

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.080
to fear for Maggie's well-being.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.100
However, Cohan has hinted that her character's
story isn't over.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:17.240
In other words, Maggie might someday make
a comeback, so don't count her out just yet.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.240
Unfriendly new faces

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:24.099
With two major characters on the way out and
a lot of time-hopping ahead, it's probably

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.720
no surprise that season 9 will introduce a
bevy of new characters.

00:06:27.969 --> 00:06:32.900
For starters, there's Samantha Morton as Alpha,
the leader of a group of creepy zombie-impersonators

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:33.820
called the Whisperers.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:38.340
She'll be joined by Ryan Hurst as Alpha's
second-in-command, Beta, and Cassady McClincy

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.680
as Lydia, Alpha's daughter.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:44.379
The show will also introduce Brett Butler
and John Finn as Tammy and Earl, a pair of

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.220
Hilltop residents.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:51.120
Meanwhile, Eleanor Matsuura and Nadia Hilker
will star as Yumiko and Magna, two more characters

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:51.940
straight from the comics.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.879
Other names joining the fold are Lauren Ridloff
as Connie and Dan Fogler as Luke.

00:06:56.879 --> 00:07:00.620
We'll just have to wait and see if any of
these new additions are able to fill the void

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.720
left by Rick and Maggie.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.340
The helicopter

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:08.480
When Rick originally saw the helicopter overhead
near the beginning of season 8, many thought

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:09.740
it was a hallucination.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:23.659
But as the tale continued to unravel, audiences
saw that the scavenger Jadis had a connection

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:24.160
to the copter.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.520
The timing of the helicopter's appearance
could be a possible introduction of the Commonwealth

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:29.880
storyline from the comics.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:34.910
However, it seems that Alpha and the Whisperers
are also on their way, so season 9 of The

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:39.020
Walking Dead might be blending multiple comic
storylines and timelines together.

00:07:39.449 --> 00:07:43.660
The addition of Alpha might finally answer
a long-lingering question about the prevalence

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.080
of the letter "A" that's been seen scattered
throughout the prior seasons.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.160
Kang has promised that the significance of
the letter will come into view in season 9,

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.920
telling fans that it might have something
to do with Jadis.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:58.180
Jadis might've made some alliances before,
but does she have another master controlling

00:07:58.199 --> 00:07:59.690
that helicopter after all?

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.899
We'll see when The Walking Dead season 9 arrives
on October 7.

